meta {
  name: List the trackers a finding can be filed into
  type: http
  seq: 12
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/organizations/{{organization_id}}/finding-tickets/trackers
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  Your connected issue trackers that can hold a ticket, such as Jira, Linear or GitHub, the one you used last first, with what each calls the place a ticket goes (`target_noun`: `team`, `project` or `repository`) and the one you used last there. `default_target` is where a new ticket goes unless you choose otherwise — the one you used last, else the one the connection’s *Issues for Incidents* setting files into — and `destination` its name as InfraNest last read it from the tracker, or null when it never has. A paused or disconnected connection is left out, so an empty list means a finding cannot be filed anywhere yet.

  Scope: `monitoring.read`
}
